//! Golden-parity tests for `build_orogeny_field`/`smooth_orogeny` (T2+T3,
//! PARITY_TESTING.md). Reference HTML lines 2981-3080 (`buildOrogenyField`/
//! `smoothOrogeny`). Golden values extracted by running the actual JS
//! functions under real Node.js (v24.19.0) with a synthetic W=20xH=14 grid,
//! one polyline per boundary type, and deterministic (non-random) stress/
//! crust/shear fields -- not hand-derived.
//!
//! `tag_boundary_types` (the per-polyline majority-vote tagging inlined in
//! JS's `currentBoundaryGraph`, reference lines 2957-2962) is intentionally
//! NOT golden-tested here: it depends on `boundaryMask`/`boundaryType`/GW/GH
//! globals a Node vm sandbox can't reach (they're `let`-scoped, not attached
//! to the context object). It's pure counting + argmax over a fixed 6-entry
//! array, matching the same "small enough to hand-trace exactly" class
//! `thin_mask`/`trace_boundaries` were tested as (T1 entry, CHANGELOG.md) --
//! verified by hand against the reference instead, see its own unit test.

